  "title": "Adaptive restoration of the former saltworks in Camargue, southern France",
  "summary": "The Salin-de Giraud restoration employs a Nature-Based Solution (NBS) approach, enhancing resilience to storms and sea level rise by restoring hydrological functions, reestablishing ecosystem characteristics, and providing breeding sites for water birds. Interventions include dredging channels, reconnecting water bodies, and abandoning seafront dykes. A large restoration project started in 2011 in the former saltworks of Salin-de Giraud, located in the southeast of the Rhône delta, within the Camargue Regional Natural Park and the UNESCO‘s Man and Biosphere Reserve.",
